Package: com.ratush.etchosts17
Name: /etc/hosts
Version: 1.0.4
Icon: file:///var/jb/Library/PreferenceBundles/EtcHosts17Prefs.bundle/SileoIcon.png
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: Real /etc/hosts for rootless jailbreaks (Dopamine). Switches on mDNSResponder's own built-in hosts engine (present in iOS but enabled only in Apple internal builds; tested on iOS 17.0, stays stock if the engine is missing) and feeds it a hosts file you edit in Settings. Entries are answered by mDNSResponder as local records before any DNS server is asked, so they win over Wi-Fi/cellular DNS, DoH/DoT profiles and VPN DNS, like hosts on Windows or Linux. No DNS profiles, no custom DNS servers, no daemons, no system settings: remove the tweak or lose the jailbreak and mDNSResponder starts stock. Green CRT editor with presets, IPv4/IPv6 and automatic A/AAAA counterparts.
Maintainer: ratush
Author: ratush
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 17.0), mobilesubstrate (>= 0.9.5000), preferenceloader
Conflicts: com.ratush.ratuhosts
Replaces: com.ratush.ratuhosts
